Run 1 (`verify --file apps/a/main.roc`): the current member is a. Only a is checked: 3 probes (the baseline, the candidate check, the build), and the `~` lines and the `--replace-dep` flags are for the uses of a only. b is not written to the plan. The note for the platform is printed once, also when 2 members change it (F5, R-SE7).
Run 2 (`verify`, no current member, R-PD5): all members are checked, a then b: 6 probes. Each candidate check has one `--replace-dep` for the platform and one for json, not one for each member that names them (F12, R-CM11). The note for the platform is printed once.
